Opt-in MCP/TCP debug server for the PCSX2 ground-truth build.

Vendors https://github.com/hkmodd/PCSX2-MCP `pcsx2-plugin/DebugServer.{cpp,h}`
(MIT) into `pcsx2/DebugTools/` of the original PCSX2 d5f75c9e4 adaptation, now applied to the
fd9d310 pin, and starts it from
VMManager::Initialize only when RRV_GT_DEBUG_SERVER is set. Applies AFTER
pcsx2-gt-capture / pcsx2-gt-guest-trace / pcsx2-vu1-input-trace /
pcsx2-gt-write-watch -- it is patch #5 in the GT stack.

  RRV_GT_DEBUG_SERVER=1        listen on TCP 21512 (the PCSX2-MCP default)
  RRV_GT_DEBUG_SERVER=<port>   listen on <port>

Default OFF: no TCP listener starts and the VSync recorder drops events.
The event hooks add only backing-state reads and branch/counter work; they do
not write guest state or change timing/IRQ/GS behavior.

What it adds over our existing instrumentation: interactive execution control
against the reference (pause / continue / step / step-over), live 128-bit
register reads across all seven categories (GPR/CP0/FPR/FCR/VU0F/VU0I/GSPRIV),
conditional execution breakpoints, PCSX2-native disassembly, expression
evaluation, and a stack walk -- i.e. the things PINE.md section 7.1 currently
documents as "open the PCSX2 GUI debugger by hand".

Five RRV edits vs upstream, all recorded in the file's provenance header:
memory accessors renamed to Read*/Write* with `bool*` validity out-params;
BiosThread::StackTop() does not exist at the pin; MipsStackWalk::Walk() takes
five arguments at the pin; the env gate; and (5) a paused-EE read-only Gate-3 event/snapshot probe.

COEXISTENCE WARNING. pcsx2-gt-write-watch.patch already changes shared memcheck
machinery -- it makes recMemcheck fire for MEMCHECK_LOG-only checks. The debug
server installs MEMCHECK_BREAK checks through the same CBreakPoints API. They
work together, but do NOT arm RRV_GT_WATCH and a debug-server watchpoint on the
same address range in one session: the aggregating histogram and the pausing
watchpoint will both claim the hit and the histogram counts become unreadable.

ORACLE WARNING. Writing guest memory or registers over this server makes the
run a modified reference, not ground truth. Read-only use only, unless the run
is explicitly labelled as an experiment.

Gate-3 commands: rrv_gt_vsync_snapshot and rrv_gt_vsync_events
(after_seq, limit<=32). Event kinds: 1 reset, 2 mode, 3 scheduled start,
4 asserted start, 5 suppressed start, 6 FIELD/VSINT, 7 suppressed FIELD,
8 asserted end, 9 suppressed end. Read while EE is paused; the ring is
16,384 records and reports overwrite and rejected-read counters. SYNCV is
read directly from PS2GS_BASE, as PCSX2 Counters.cpp itself does. CMOD is
SMODE1 bits 13-14; VFP odd is SYNCV bit 0. video_mode is the timing-cache
mode, while gs_video_mode and gs_is_interlaced are live counter inputs.
Initial hwReset calls rcntInit before DebugServer::Start in VM initialization;
therefore its Reset event is absent from the ring (later resets can record).

